\description{
Get ESPN's play-by-play win-probability series for a single
college football game -- one row per play.
}
\details{
Wraps the paginated ESPN core-v2 endpoint
\code{events/{game_id}/competitions/{game_id}/probabilities}. The endpoint
is paginated; this wrapper loops every page and stacks the results into
one frame -- one row per play, each carrying the home / away / tie win
percentages at that point in the game, plus spread-cover and total
(over/under) probabilities. \code{play_id} is parsed from each row's play
\verb{$ref} so the series can be joined to \code{\link[=espn_cfb_game_pbp]{espn_cfb_game_pbp()}}.

This endpoint responds \verb{HTTP 400} for future / not-yet-played games and
is only populated for \strong{completed} games. The \verb{@examples} use a finished
game; pass \code{game_id} values for completed games.

When \code{team_detail = TRUE} (the default) the ESPN team catalog
(\code{\link[=espn_cfb_teams]{espn_cfb_teams()}}) is fetched once and friendly team fields are joined
in next to both the \code{home_team_id} and \code{away_team_id} columns -- e.g.
\code{home_team_name}, \code{home_team_abbreviation}, ..., \code{away_team_name},
\code{away_team_abbreviation}, .... A catalog failure degrades to \code{NA} rather
than erroring the wrapper. Set \code{team_detail = FALSE} to skip the catalog
fetch and the join.
}
